  "question": {
    "text": "The electrical resistance $R$ of a conductor of length $l$ and area of cross section $a$ is given by $R=\\frac{\\rho l}{a}$ where ' $\\rho$ ' is the electrical resistivity. What is the dimensional formula for electrical conductivity ' $\\sigma$ ' which is reciprocal of resistivity?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nxjB0",
      "text": "\n$\\left[M^{-1} L^{-3} T^3 A^2\\right]$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "KxegJ",
      "text": "\n$\\left[M L^{-3} T^{-3} A^2\\right]$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fNFBS",
      "text": "\n$\\left[M L^3 T^{-3} A^{-2}\\right]$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uR9ag",
      "text": "\n$\\left[M^{-2} L^3 T^2 A^{-1}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Dimensional formula for electrical resistivity, $\\rho=\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^3 \\mathrm{~T}^{-3} \\mathrm{~A}^{-2}\\right]$ Dimensional formula for electrical conductivity, $\\sigma=\\frac{1}{\\rho}$ is $\\left[\\mathrm{M}^{-1} \\mathrm{~L}^{-3} \\mathrm{~T}^3 \\mathrm{~A}^2\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
